            "\\(x = 60^{\\circ}, 120^{\\circ}\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "hint": "Take the square root to get \\(\\sin x = \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\). All 4 quadrants are valid.",
          "solution": "\\(x = 60^{\\circ}, 120^{\\circ}, 240^{\\circ}, 300^{\\circ}\\)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Take the square root of both sides. Remember to include both positive and negative roots.",
              "work": "\\(\\sin x = \\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"
